.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-WIFI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-wifi
.Nd the WiFi networks this machine knows
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list | scan | status | iface
.Nm
.Cm scan Fl -tsv
.Nm
.Cm add Ar ssid Oo Fl -wpa2-only Oc Op Fl -stdin
.Nm
.Cm forget Ar ssid
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
manages the credentials in
.Pa /etc/novi/wifi.conf ,
which is
wpa_supplicant(8) Ns 's
own format, mode 0600 and root-only.
.Pp
Turning the radio on and off is declared state rather than a command
here:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-state set network.wifi on
# novi-state apply
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "add ssid --wpa2-only"
.It Cm list
Networks this machine has credentials for.
.It Cm add Ar ssid
Add one, prompting for the passphrase.
.It Cm add Ar ssid Fl -stdin
The same, reading the passphrase from standard input.
This exists so a GUI can add a network without a terminal.
The passphrase is never an argument, because an argument is
world-readable in
.Pa /proc/ Ns Ar pid Ns Pa /cmdline
for as long as the process lives.
.It Cm add Ar ssid Fl -wpa2-only
Store only the derived PSK.
.It Cm forget Ar ssid
Remove one.
.It Cm scan
What is on the air now.
.It Cm scan Fl -tsv
The same as
.Ar signal Ns \(ti Ns Ar ssid ,
signal first, because an SSID may contain spaces and a trailing field
cannot be found by counting from the left.
.It Cm status
What the supplicant is doing.
.It Cm iface
The wireless interface's name, if there is one.
.El
.Ss WPA3 and the passphrase on disk
A network added normally works on WPA2, WPA3 transition mode and
WPA3-only, which means the plaintext passphrase is stored alongside
the derived PSK: SAE derives from the passphrase, not from the PSK, so
there is no one-way transform to store instead.
.Fl -wpa2-only
stores only the PSK, for anyone who would rather keep a reused
passphrase out of the file than reach a WPA3-only network.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/novi/wifi.conf" -compact
.It Pa /etc/novi/wifi.conf
Credentials, mode 0600.
See
.Xr wifi.conf 5 .
.It Pa /run/novi/network.wifi.device
The interface the service resolved, published for readers such as the
panel.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-wifi scan
# novi-wifi add "Cafe WiFi"
# novi-state set network.wifi on && novi-state apply
# novi-wifi status
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-state 1 ,
.Xr system.conf 5 ,
.Xr wifi.conf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0009 and RFC 0021.
.Sh CAVEATS
Enterprise (802.1X) networks are not supported.
